      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:18upktw'
    '|b||Amartya Sen put it bluntly in 1970: a society can be Pareto optimal and still be perfectly disgusting.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ib1i5q'
    '|a||Liv has three fish, Tor has three, and four rot on the quay. Which split is a Pareto improvement on that?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Three for Liv, seven for Tor: Liv keeps her three and Tor gains four. The other two cost Tor fish.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8120
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So efficiency rules out waste, and nothing else. Who gets the fish is a different question.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Pareto''s test never takes a fish from anyone. That sounds harmless, until you notice that almost every real policy has a loser.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Say the harbour council builds a breakwater, and the day''s catch grows from ten fish to twelve. Illustrative numbers again.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1eup3af'
    '|b||Liv''s berth gets the shelter: she goes from five fish to eight. Tor''s gets worse: from five to four.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:199vtiq'
    '|a||Two more fish in total, but Tor is down one. So it''s not a Pareto improvement, and under Pareto''s rule one loser blocks it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1qz9wn0'
    '|b||In 1939 Nicholas Kaldor and John Hicks proposed a looser test: could the winners compensate the losers and still come out ahead?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:10e5zuy'
    '|a||Here they could. Liv hands Tor one fish back: seven and five, and nobody is worse off than before the breakwater.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:m4398l'
    '|b||That''s a potential Pareto improvement, and it''s the logic behind cost-benefit analysis. But could isn''t did: if Liv keeps the fish, Tor is still down one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:mp4i9g'
    '|a||And in 1941 Tibor Scitovsky showed the looser test can approve a move, and then approve the move back again.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ihbv91'
    '|b||So how sure are we? That Pareto efficiency only rules out waste and says nothing about fairness: consensus.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1gt7f92'
    '|a||Whether a compensation that''s never paid should count as a gain: contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:3gwvq5'
    '|b||There''s a compact way to write both tests. Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1dafqo0'
    '|a||A split x is Pareto efficient if no feasible split y gives everyone at least as much, and someone more.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Kaldor and Hicks ask less: add up the gains and losses, and the sum must be positive.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1edr0pt'
    '|a||The breakwater: Liv plus three, Tor minus one, a sum of plus two. It passes, though Tor loses.':
